cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AI Safety from Zero to the Open Frontier
message: >-
  If you refer to this book, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: A.
    given-names: Mohammed Sharukh
    affiliation: >-
      MSc Mathematics, Indian Institute of Technology Palakkad
abstract: >-
  A problem-driven tour of AI safety, grounded in landmark original papers, in
  which every printed number is computed on a single five-state Markov decision
  process in exact rational arithmetic and carries a receipt naming the check
  that produced it. Ten chapters, each identifying a distinct mechanism by which
  a measured quantity and an intended one come apart. Exposition of published
  results, not original research; written in collaboration with Claude
  (Anthropic), as disclosed in the book.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - AI alignment
  - reward specification
  - Goodhart's law
  - reinforcement learning
  - interpretability
  - scalable oversight
